### UC01 – Request Tour Booking (happy path)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "tour-alpine-001",
  "tourDate": "2026-06-15",
  "participantCount": 2,
  "contactName": "Klaus Kinsky",
  "contactEmail": "kinsky@example.com"
}

### UC01 – Validation error: past date (400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "tour-alpine-001",
  "tourDate": "2020-01-01",
  "participantCount": 2,
  "contactName": "Max Mustermann",
  "contactEmail": "max@example.com"
}

### UC01 – Validation error: participantCount below minimum (400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "tour-alpine-001",
  "tourDate": "2026-06-15",
  "participantCount": 0,
  "contactName": "Max Mustermann",
  "contactEmail": "max@example.com"
}

### UC01 – Validation error: missing required fields (400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "",
  "tourDate": "2026-06-15",
  "participantCount": 1,
  "contactName": "",
  "contactEmail": ""
}

### UC01 – Error: capacity exceeded (409)
# NOT REPRODUCIBLE LOCALLY. CapacityExceededException maps to 409, but
# StubAvailabilityChecker returns AvailableCapacity(Integer.MAX_VALUE), so no
# participantCount can exceed it and this request returns 201.
# To exercise it, bind an AvailabilityChecker with finite capacity in
# bootstrap/BookingConfig. Covered by
# TourBookingTest.participantCountExceedingCapacityThrowsCapacityExceededException,
# RequestTourBookingDriverTest.capacityExceeded_throwsCapacityExceededExceptionAndSaveNotCalled
# and TourBookingControllerTest.postWithCapacityExceeded_returns409.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "tour-alpine-001",
  "tourDate": "2026-06-15",
  "participantCount": 999,
  "contactName": "Max Mustermann",
  "contactEmail": "max@example.com"
}

### UC01 – Error: availability check failure (502)
# NOT REPRODUCIBLE LOCALLY. AvailabilityUnavailableException maps to 502, but the
# local StubAvailabilityChecker never fails, so this request returns 201.
# To exercise it, replace the StubAvailabilityChecker binding in
# bootstrap/BookingConfig with an implementation that throws
# AvailabilityUnavailableException. Covered by
# RequestTourBookingDriverTest.availabilityFailure_propagatesExceptionAndSaveNotCalled
# and TourBookingControllerTest.postWithAvailabilityFailure_returns502.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "tour-alpine-001",
  "tourDate": "2026-06-15",
  "participantCount": 2,
  "contactName": "Max Mustermann",
  "contactEmail": "max@example.com"
}